 "note": "Success spec for a Phase-C3 run that reached ALL_DONE. Every pattern is a path the STANDALONE C1 driver writes: audit/autoinit_c3, stage3/c3/<probe_id>, eval/c3/<probe_id>. The previous version of this file named audit/autoinit_phase_a, stage3/phase_a and eval/phase_a, because the driver then inherited PhaseADriver and wrote there; that driver has been replaced and those paths no longer exist for C1. Counts: 9 probes = 3 arms x 3 seeds; 63 = 9 x the 7 sets of c1_confirmation_v1, because uncapped_eval writes one <set>.generations.jsonl and one <set>.json per set — requiring 9 would accept a probe that generated one set out of seven. Entries are ArtifactSpec kwargs; the manifest root is artifacts/. FULL SUCCESS NEEDS BOTH ARM RECORDS. c3_replay_record.json is the incumbent arm's replay against two frozen digests; c3_B_causal_b1_record.json is the treatment arm's verified-suffix execution, whose output digest was never pinned and which is therefore NOT a replay. Requiring only the first would let a session that reached ALL_DONE come home without any record of how the treatment arm was built — which arm-identities alone does not supply, because it names the output and not the verified prefix it came from. C3 NOTE: THREE arms, so both causal arms owe a verified-suffix execution record -- c3_B_causal_b1_record.json and c3_C_causal_b3_record.json. Requiring only one would let a session come home with no record of how the other treatment was built, which arm-identities alone does not supply because it names the output and not the verified prefix it came from.",
